                <pb facs="0217" n="93" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg93"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862i.01/68</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wallace</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-03-03"><hi rendition="#italic">March 3,
                        1921</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received March 16.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2209</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In confirmation of my telegram No. 156,
                    March 1, 8 p.m.,<anchor n="7" xml:id="d106-f1"/> I have the honor to enclose
                    herewith a copy and English translation of a note dated March 1, from His
                    Excellency Senhor Gastao da Cunha, President of the Council of the League of
                        Nations,<anchor n="7" xml:id="d106-f2"/> transmitting the reply—the original
                    text of which is likewise enclosed herewith—of the Council to your communication
                    of February 21st last.</p>
                <p>There is also enclosed herewith a copy and translation of my note<anchor n="7"
                        xml:id="d106-f3"/> in reply to the aforementioned letter of Mr. da Cunha,
                    dated March 3rd, 1921, in accordance with the instructions contained in your
                    telegram No. 127, March 2, 12 a.m.<anchor n="7" xml:id="d106-f4"/></p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hugh C. Wallace</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d106-a1.xml" xpointer="d106-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
